    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Run chroma color matting on a target segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --color TEXT        Key color to remove, e.g. #00FF00FF (#RRGGBBAA)\r\n          --intensity TEXT    Normalized keying intensity in [0,1] or 0%-100%\r\n          --shadow TEXT       Shadow strength, numeric (0.0 - 1.0)\r\n          --edge-smooth TEXT  Edge smoothing, numeric (0.0 - 1.0)\r\n          --spill TEXT        Spill removal, numeric (0.0 - 1.0)\r\n          --path TEXT         Chroma resource package path; defaults to bundled Chroma2\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Key out a green screen color\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo chroma-color-matting --seg-id <UUID> --color #00FF00FF\r\n  # Key out with fine-tuned intensity / shadow / edge / spill\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo chroma-color-matting --seg-id <UUID> --color #00FF00FF \\\r\n      --intensity 0.8 --shadow 0.2 --edge-smooth 0.3 --spill 0.4\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Run chroma color matting on a target segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --color TEXT        Key color to remove, e.g. #00FF00FF (#RRGGBBAA)\r\n          --intensity TEXT    Normalized keying intensity in [0,1] or 0%-100%\r\n          --shadow TEXT       Shadow strength, numeric (0.0 - 1.0)\r\n          --edge-smooth TEXT  Edge smoothing, numeric (0.0 - 1.0)\r\n          --spill TEXT        Spill removal, numeric (0.0 - 1.0)\r\n          --path TEXT         Chroma resource package path; defaults to bundled Chroma2\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Key out a green screen color\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo chroma-color-matting --seg-id <UUID> --color #00FF00FF\r\n  # Key out with fine-tuned intensity / shadow / edge / spill\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo chroma-color-matting --seg-id <UUID> --color #00FF00FF \\\r\n      --intensity 0.8 --shadow 0.2 --edge-smooth 0.3 --spill 0.4\r\n",
